# ollama — a local ollama instance running on the host (agentic framework: any)
#
# Reaches the host over plain HTTP on a non-standard port (default 11434) via
# the docker host-gateway. Two things make this work and both live in tracked
# config, not in this list:
#   - docker-compose.yml maps host.docker.internal -> host-gateway on the
#     firewall container;
#   - firewall/dnsmasq.conf omits `no-hosts`, so dnsmasq serves that
#     /etc/hosts entry to the development container's resolver.
# Squid still brokers the connection, so this list is what actually permits it.
# Off by default — opt in with `fw feature on ollama`.
host.docker.internal
